    "rationale": "I diluted the 18 h aliquot 10-fold and got 0.1264 and 0.1230. Multiplying by 10 gives about 1.25, which is close to the undiluted reading of 1.29. I diluted the 12 h aliquot 20-fold and got 0.0766 and 0.0652. Multiplying by 20 gives about 1.42, compared with 1.30 undiluted. The two replicates at 12 h differ by about 16%, so this value is uncertain and is consistent with the reading. If the reader were saturating, the diluted samples scaled back up would come out well above the undiluted readings. They don't. So the plateau near 1.3 is real stationary phase, not a reader ceiling."
